  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1159 PM CST Fri Nov 13 2026\n\nWell defined upper level low will pivot across Oklahoma and north \nTexas during the day on Sunday before moving into the ArkLaTex \nSunday night. Showers and thunderstorms will continue in the morning \nhours, with the bulk of the activity exiting the area to the east in \nthe afternoon. Will hold onto some rain chances in the evening \nmainly in the Big Country as the upper low moves overhead. Rain \nchances come to an end on Monday as upper level ridging builds \ninto the region from the west. Temperatures on Sunday will be \nchilly in the Big Country due to expected cloud cover/rain and low\nlevel east-northeast flow. Temperatures further south into the \nConcho Valley and northern Edwards Plateau will be in the 60s and \n70s. Below normal temperatures will prevail area wide on Monday \nas cool surface high pressure builds into the area from the north.\nTemperatures will then gradually warm back up into the 60s and \n70s through the end of the work week. Low end rain chances return \nto the forecast on Thursday and Friday.",
